step("login", "Refresh (proactive or reactive)", "background",
     "Nothing visible on a healthy session — this is what keeps a long session alive without asking the user to log in every 5 minutes.",
     "Call this either on a timer set just under the 5-minute access-token lifetime, or reactively the first time any protected call returns 401. Coordinate concurrent callers onto ONE in-flight refresh (see the reference code) — never fire five parallel refresh calls because five requests happened to 401 at the same instant.",
     "Nothing.",
     "POST", "/api/v1/auth/refresh/",
     ["The HttpOnly refresh_token cookie must be present and valid — the browser sends it automatically; the frontend never reads or constructs it."],
     {"headers": "X-CSRFToken: <csrfToken>", "body": None, "query": None},
     {"status": 200, "body": {"access": "eyJhbGciOi..."}, "note": "Only a new access token — no user object here, unlike login."},
     "A new access token, replacing the old one in memory. The cookie is also silently rotated by the response (Set-Cookie) — nothing to do on the frontend for that part.",
     "Whichever request originally 401'd is retried exactly once with the new token.",
     {"loading": "Invisible — this must never show its own spinner; the ORIGINAL request's loading state is what the user sees.",
      "empty": "Not applicable.",
      "success": "Original failed request is retried transparently.",
      "error": "401 here (missing/expired/blacklisted cookie, or the user was deactivated) means the session is genuinely over — force logout, clear all in-memory and cached state, return to AUTH-01. Do not loop."},
     ["Waiting past the access-token lifetime and then performing an action still works without the user noticing (proactive refresh), or",
      "Manually expiring the in-memory access token and performing an action triggers exactly one refresh + one retry, verified in the network tab (reactive refresh)",
      "Firing several requests at once right after expiry results in exactly ONE refresh call, not one per request"],
     ["apps/authentication/views.py (RefreshView)"])

